TAMLINUX-TOOLS

Standalone Tamlinux command-line utilities written in pure C against libtam
<https://github.com/greenermoose/libtam>. Each tool is a small program with
its own component version, delivered through tamlinux-packages
<https://github.com/greenermoose/tamlinux-packages> assemblies, and usable
from scripts without the Tamlinux desktop shell.


WHAT BELONGS HERE

A tool belongs in this repository when it is:

- Implemented in pure C and linked against libtam (and libtam-portal only when
  the tool needs the desktop portal)
- Small and reusable from other programs or shell scripts
- Independent of the Tamlinux Quickshell shell, compositor adapters, and
  product menus
- Versioned with this component, not with the Tamlinux product number

Bash or Python scripts are not added here. Rewrite them in C with libtam first
if they should become tools in this suite.


WHAT BELONGS ELSEWHERE

  Need: Workstation / product tam-* commands (menus, theme, deploy, compositor
  helpers, lifecycle tools)
  Repository: tamlinux <https://github.com/greenermoose/tamlinux> under
  commands/

  Need: Offline knowledge browser and guide pager
  Repository: tam <https://github.com/greenermoose/tam>

  Need: Shared C foundation library
  Repository: libtam <https://github.com/greenermoose/libtam>

  Need: Package recipes and assembly pins
  Repository: tamlinux-packages
  <https://github.com/greenermoose/tamlinux-packages>


TOOLS

  Command: tam-file-select
  Description: File chooser via the desktop XDG Portal
  Dependencies: Static libtam-portal / libtam; shared libdbus-1 at runtime

  Command: tam-journal
  Description: Plain-text daily journal in Micro
  Dependencies: Static libtam 0.8.0 or later

Source installs place tam-file-select and tam-journal on PATH. Product flows
that call tam-file-select include share (tam-menu-share) and theme branding
image pick.


DAILY TEXT JOURNAL

tam-journal [add] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] edits a day in Micro; add starts a blank
note that is appended after saving and closing. Files are ordinary UTF-8 text
under ~/Journal/YYYY-MM-DD.txt, configurable with the absolute
TAM_JOURNAL_DIR. Quick notes carry the actual capture timestamp and zone.
Private drafts, per-day locks and atomic writes protect existing text;
failures retain the draft and print its path. See man tam-journal and the
design <docs/plans/plain-text-journal.md>. make test-journal runs its isolated
behavior checks. The product supplies calendar/Quick Launch entry points; this
command also works on a text console. Journal data is outside package
rollback. This adds no daemon, sync service or database.


USAGE: tam-file-select

    tam-file-select [--title <title>] [--multiple] [--directory] [--extensions "<ext ext...>"]

Prints selected path(s), one per line. Exit 0 on pick, 1 if nothing was
picked, 2 if the chooser failed to open.


BUILDING AND INSTALLATION

Links statically against an installed libtam 0.8.0 or later. tam-file-select
uses the portal library via pkg-config libtam-portal (adds libtam and D-Bus).
Install libtam first; if its prefix is outside pkg-config's default path:

    export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$HOME/.local/lib/pkgconfig"

    make
    make test
    sudo make install PREFIX=/usr/local

Development install for your user (make uninstall with the same PREFIX):

    make install PREFIX=$HOME/.local

Or name the libtam prefix without pkg-config:

    make LIBTAM_PREFIX=/path/to/libtam

Portability notes for musl or other distributions belong with libtam; this
repo does not claim measured cold-start times or verified musl builds.


